    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "With `app.staticFiles(\"/\", root)`, `GET /` returns the bytes of `root/index.html` and `GET /assets/app.js` returns the bytes of `root/assets/app.js`, both `200`. [D-256; T27]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 278
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "`GET /docs/` returns `root/docs/index.html`, and with `index(\"main.html\")` it returns `root/docs/main.html` instead. [D-257; D-261; T27]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 279
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "With the mounts `/` on `rootA` and `/static` on `rootB`, `GET /static/x.css` returns `rootB/x.css` and `GET /a.txt` returns `rootA/a.txt`; with `spaFallback(true)` on the `/` mount, `GET /static/x.css` with `Accept: text/html` still returns `rootB/x.css`, and `GET /static/missing.css` with `Accept: text/html` receives the SPA index of the `/` mount. Decision: mounts are consulted in registration order and a miss in one mount falls through to the next, as with several Express `static` middlewares; SPA fallback runs only after every mount missed the file lookup, and then the first registered mount with `spaFallback(true)` whose prefix matches the path serves its index. [D-258; D-265]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 280
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
        "text": "With an explicit `GET /index.html` route and a `/` mount whose root holds `index.html`, `GET /index.html` returns the route's body. [D-259; T27]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 281
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-5",
        "text": "A global middleware registered through `app.use` that sets `X-Mw: 1` runs on `GET /assets/app.js` served from a mount, the response carries `X-Mw: 1`, a global middleware that ends the response itself prevents the file from being sent, and one access-log line is written for the static request. [D-407; T35]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 282
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-6",
        "text": "`GET /docs?x=1` for the directory `root/docs` is answered `301` with `Location: /docs/?x=1`; `GET /my%20docs` is answered `301` with `Location: /my%20docs/` built from the raw encoded path; and `GET //assets` is answered `404`, so no `Location` starts with `//` (a T29 case). [wave decision: SPA fallback exclusions; D-267; T29] Decision: the `301` applies to `GET` and `HEAD` of a directory without a trailing `/`, with `Location` equal to the raw path plus `/` plus `?` and the raw query when a query is present. [SDS 2026-10-19.naruserve.naruserve-v1-wave-6-6 SDS-AC-4]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 283
      }
    ],
