    "requirement": "The system shall map `prefix + relative path` of a static mount to the file under its directory, serve the configured index file for a directory path ending in `/`, let several mounts with different prefixes coexist, consult static mounts only after explicit routes, run global middleware on requests that end in a static file, and redirect a directory request without a trailing slash with `301` to the same path plus `/`.",
    "rationale": "Covers D-256, D-257, D-258, D-259, D-407 (T27, T35) and the trailing-slash part of D-267 settled by the wave decision \"SPA fallback exclusions\" (W2-009; `serve-static` behaviour; CVE-2015-1164 open redirect avoided by building `Location` from the raw path and answering `404` for an empty segment; r2 W2-001). Builds on FR-HTTP-022 (fallback point after the route lookup), FR-APP-003 (global middleware) and FR-APP-015 (one access-log line per request).",
